'''''Rhododendron molle''''' (羊踯躅) is a [[rhododendron]] [[species]] native to [[China]] and [[Japan]], where it grows at altitudes of sea level to 2500 meters. This [[deciduous]] shrub grows to {{convert|50-200|cm|in|abbr=on}} in height, with leaves that are oblong to oblong-[[lanceolate]], 5–11 by 1.5–3.5&nbsp;cm in size. The flowers are yellow with dark red flecks.

This azalea is not often seen in cultivation, but is the parent of many yellow-flowered [[hybrid (biology)#In plants|hybrid]]s.<ref name = TSO>{{cite web | url = https://treesandshrubsonline.org/articles/rhododendron/rhododendron-molle/ | title = ''Rhododendron molle'' | website = Trees and Shrubs Online | publisher = International Dendrology Society  | access-date = 22 April 2021}}</ref>

